I left out both operations requests. The node's declared capabilities are only `StateHandle<'seen', read>`, and `wasm32-unknown-unknown` has no filesystem. An HTTP import would also send untrusted feed text to an external host outside the graph's declared capabilities. If operations needs logging or enrichment, it should go in a separate node that declares those capabilities in the graph, or on the host side.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{feed-item};

    import aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(items: list<feed-item>) -> list<feed-item>;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(items: Vec<FeedItem>) -> Vec<FeedItem> {
        items
            .into_iter()
            .filter(|item| crate::aap::caps::state_read::get(&item.id).is_none())
            .collect()
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

